# Optional config file for the Windows test-deploy build (dist-bin/teabox.exe).
#
# Copy this file next to teabox.exe and rename it to "config.env" to customize it.
# If no config.env is present, teabox.exe runs with the defaults commented out below.
# This file (once renamed) travels with teabox.exe and teabox.db as one portable set
# — safe to keep all three together on a USB drive or in one folder on the PC.

# Port the app listens on. Change this only if 4000 is already used by something
# else on the target machine.
#PORT=4000

# Signs login sessions (JWT). You normally don't need to set this: a fresh install
# with no JWT_SECRET configured generates a random one on first run and saves it as
# jwt-secret next to teabox.exe, so it's reused across restarts automatically. Set
# your own here only if you want a specific value (e.g. restoring onto a fresh
# machine without carrying over the generated jwt-secret file — losing that file just
# means everyone has to log in again, nothing else). Never ship a real deploy with a
# hardcoded/shared value here.
#JWT_SECRET=change-me-to-something-random

# Loopback-only (127.0.0.1) by default, so a fresh install isn't reachable from other
# devices on the shop's network until someone opts in on purpose. Set to 0.0.0.0 to
# accept connections from other devices (e.g. a second register) — this app has no
# TLS of its own, so put a TLS-terminating reverse proxy in front of it before doing
# that on any network you don't fully trust.
#HOST=127.0.0.1

# Normally irrelevant for the packaged .exe: the web client is served from the same
# origin/port as the API, so the browser never makes a cross-origin request that
# would need this. Only matters if you point a browser at this API from elsewhere.
#CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# Optional: skip the manual Setup Wizard entirely on a fresh (empty) teabox.db by
# providing the store/owner details here instead of typing them into the browser
# form. Useful for repeatable test deploys where you want the same known owner login
# every time. All four required vars must be set together — a partial set is treated
# as a mistake and falls back to the manual wizard (see server/src/services/
# setup.service.ts's maybeAutoCompleteSetup). Has no effect once a store already
# exists in teabox.db, so it's safe to leave these set across restarts.
#SETUP_STORE_NAME=My Resale Shop
#SETUP_STORE_LOCATION=Springfield, IL
#SETUP_OWNER_NAME=Jane Owner
#SETUP_OWNER_EMAIL=owner@example.com
#SETUP_OWNER_PASSWORD=change-me-to-something-real
